t also kill any tracked survivors (background daemons left by tests) and count them. (5) Metrics: in the existing command_metrics ContextVar dict record peak_rss_bytes (max over commands), mem_kills, orphan_kills; and have eval/kaggle/gold_calibration.py write peak_rss_bytes, mem_kills, orphan_kills into each result row (numbers only, never task text) and log one line per task. Also add env GOLD_CONCURRENCY (default keep current 2) so a local run can use 1. (6) Must keep working with bwrap (--unshare-pid: inner processes are visible in host /proc with host pids) and without bwrap (hidden_paths empty). Tests: new eval/tests/test_sandbox_limits.py: (a) timeout with an orphaning grandchild via bash '(sleep 600 &); sleep 600' and a setsid'd grandchild via python os.setsid -> status timeout, exit 124, zero survivors; (b) memory: a child allocating ~600 MB in touched steps with GEMMA_SANDBOX_MEM_BYTES=300MB -> killed, 137, mem_kills=1; (c) normal command output/exit code identical to the original executor's for a few commands (echo, exit 3, stderr), peak_rss_bytes>0; (d) background daemon left after normal exit is killed and counted. Keep every test allocation <= 1 GB and test wall time < 60 s. Run ONLY eval/tests/test_sandbox_limits.py and eval/tests/test_eval_fixes.py plus eval/tests/test_gold_calibration.py (python: /home/ubuntu/gemma-local/venv/bin/python3 with /home/ubuntu/gemma-local/pyimg/cpython-3.13.18-linux-x86_64-gnu/lib/python3.13/site-packages appended to sys.path, then pytest.main); do not run the full suite or any real gold calibration. No new dependencies.
